{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>This month.</b> The month is called חדש and ירח on account of the renewal of the moon's light." "<b>This.</b> This is Nisan, for since it says ״חג האסיף תקופת השנה״ (the festival of ingathering, at the turn of the year) and ״וחג האסיף בצאת השנה״ (and the festival of ingathering at the going out of the year) — go and see which month has in it the festival of ingathering and the turn of the year, such that the year goes out in it and it is called the seventh, as it explains in the perasha of Emor: ״אך בחמשה עשר יום לחדש השביעי הזה באספכם את תבואת הארץ וגו׳״ — you find none other than the month of Tishrei. Once you have learned that the seventh is Tishrei, Nisan will be the first. And even though there is no proof for this, it is a remembrance: ״בחדש הראשון״ — this is the month of Nisan." "<b>This.</b> Moses was perplexed by it, because the molad of that Nisan did not appear until eighteen hours into the fourth day, and it was very thin. So the liturgical poet established: ״ועד שלשים מחצות לא ניכר בחוצות״ (and until thirty and a half [hours], it was not discernible in the streets). Another interpretation: he was perplexed as to when the month may be sanctified — whether when the moon's concavity is toward the north or when it is toward the south — until HaShem said to him: ״כזה ראה וקדש״ (like this, see and sanctify). That is: when the moon is in its renewal, its concavity is below as it grows and rises and its face is toward the north; and when it is old, its concavity is above as it grows and rises and its face is toward the south." "<b>For you.</b> And not for other nations, for they count by the sun." "<b>Head of the months.</b> But not for years, for shemittot and for yovelot, for planting and for vegetables. As it is said: ״מקץ שבע שנים במועד שנת השמיטה בחג הסוכות״ (at the end of seven years, at the appointed time of the shemittah year, on the festival of Sukkot). And if Nisan were established to be the head of the year, why did HaShem not command to read in the Torah on the festival of matzot? And further, we find ״חג האסיף תקופת השנה״ and ״חג האסיף בצאת השנה״ — to teach you that from there the year begins its beginning." "<b>ראש חדשים (head of months).</b> I might have understood [this as referring to] a paucity of months — [only two or three]; therefore Scripture says לחדשי השנה (for the months of the year)." "<b>ראשון הוא (it is first).</b> As it is written, שמור את חדש האביב וגו׳ (Observe the month of the aviv, etc.) — lest you say [one might] skip Nisan; rather, if you say so, you would make Nisan second, and the Torah says ראשון לכם — first to you, to begin with it the counting of the months of the year, whether [the year] has twelve months or whether it has thirteen months, for we do not find any prohibition in the Torah against counting only twelve months; but we do find it written to perform the Pesach and to call 'the first month' the month in which aviv occurs, and to perform Shavuot at a time when they can offer in it the first fruits of wheat." "<b>ראשון הוא לכם (it is first for you).</b> From here onward it is first — because when you count the months from the time of freedom, you will remember the kindness I did with you; but from the first man until now, Tishrei is first and Nisan is seventh, as it is written in Kings בירח האיתנים בחג (in the month of the mighty ones, at the festival), and Targum Yonatan translates: בירחא דעתיקיא קרו ליה ירחא קדמאה וכען הוא ירחא שביעאה — 'the ancient month they called the first month, and now it is the seventh month.'" "<b>לחדשי השנה (for the months of the year).</b> Nisan is first, Iyyar is second, Sivan is third. And all the names of the months are not in the sacred language but in the Chaldean language; therefore you will not find a single one of them anywhere in Scripture except in the books of Haggai, Zechariah, Daniel, and Esther, because all of these were in exile. But we do find in Scripture that [some months] are called by other names: ירח זיו, בירח האיתנים, ירח בול."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:57:18.118722637Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}